From zamora at ebi.ac.uk  Thu Aug  5 14:35:53 2010
From: zamora at ebi.ac.uk (jorge zamora)
Date: Thu, 05 Aug 2010 13:35:53 +0100
Subject: [BioC] clarification on MULTI SPECIES COMPARISONS filters
Message-ID: <1281011753.2419.78.camel@jorge-laptop>

Hello bioconductor list,

This is a clarification on MULTI SPECIES COMPARISONS filters in Ensembl
Genes Mart raised by an user query. Currently (release 58) the only
filters available restrict on the genes retrieved by only including or
excluding homolog and paralog genes. As far as I concerned this
limitation will be the same on biomaRt. Thus I don't think it's possible
to filter in biomaRt by for instance 'dN', 'dS' which  currently are
only present in Ensembl Genes Mart as attributes.

Hope this helps.

Many thanks,
Jorge.


From Julie.Zhu at umassmed.edu  Thu Aug  5 15:58:43 2010
From: Julie.Zhu at umassmed.edu (Zhu, Julie)
Date: Thu, 5 Aug 2010 09:58:43 -0400
Subject: [BioC] ChIPpeakAnno:write2FASTA, getAllPeakSequence Functions
In-Reply-To: <572A6D0E-3D00-456C-A896-3817476C35A3@ucla.edu>
Message-ID: <C8803BD3.2C86%julie.zhu@umassmed.edu>

Dear Noah,

Thanks so much for sharing your example and excellent solution!

Yes, if you create your RangedData with names field, then the sequences will
have names associated with, that are used by write2FASTA as sequence
headers. In the future release, headers could be automatically generated if
no head found. 

Here is the example to create a RangedData with names field filled in.
 peaks = RangedData(IRanges(start=c(100, 500), end=c(300, 600),
names=c("peak1", "peak2")), space=c("NC_008253", "NC_010468"))
    library(BSgenome.Ecoli.NCBI.20080805)
     seq = getAllPeakSequence(peaks, upstream = 20,
    downstream = 20, genome = Ecoli)
    write2FASTA(seq)

Thanks so much for the positive feedback!

Kind regards,

Julie


