Dear David,

limma doesn't work with only one gene.  In principle, it should give the 
same results as lm when there is only one row of data.  In practice, it 
fails for a purely technical programming issue -- R by default converts 
single row matrices into vectors, and this confuses limma which is 
expecting to get matrices.  We could fix this, but no one has ever asked 
for it before!

Best wishes
Gordon


