I get the exact same image from your heatmap.2 plot as when I plot an image
of 
your scaled matrix "stdizedmat":

a <- heatmap.2(toy.mat,
     Rowv=T, Colv=T,
     distfun=dist.pear,
     hclustfun=hclust.ave,
     scale= "row",
     col=greenred(256),
     breaks = c(seq(-2, 2, length.out = 257)),
     trace="none",
     density.info="none",
     main="heatmap.2 clustered"
   ) ##will produce heatmap image

row.order<-a$rowInd
col.order<-a$colInd

windows()
image(t(stdizedmat[row.order,col.order]),zlim=c(-clipper,clipper), 
col=greenred(256)) ##same image as before

...so I don't think it actually does mess up the scaling in this case.

Elizabeth


